WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.056
Here's how to connect Slack to Sessionboard, so your team can ask about your events without leaving Slack, and get Sessionboard notifications there too. You connect once for the organization. Open Apps from the left sidebar, and click Slack.

2
00:00:16.856 --> 00:00:31.208
Click Set up Slack, give the connection a name, and click Connect with Slack. Slack asks you to allow Sessionboard into your workspace. Check it's the right workspace, click Allow, and you'll see Connected.

3
00:00:32.008 --> 00:00:45.064
Now open Sessionboard in Slack, from your apps or from Agents and tools. This is its chat. You'll see a few suggested questions based on your recent events, or you can just type your own.

4
00:00:45.864 --> 00:00:59.664
Ask the way you'd ask a colleague. Here, how many speakers have confirmed for one event. Sessionboard looks it up and answers right in the conversation, and follow-up questions keep the context.

5
00:01:00.464 --> 00:01:17.624
In any channel or direct message, type slash Sessionboard and your question. That answer is visible only to you. You can also mention Sessionboard in a channel it's been added to, and it replies in a thread that the whole channel can read.

6
00:01:18.424 --> 00:01:32.392
Every answer runs under the asking person's own Sessionboard permissions, matched by their Slack email. And in your notification preferences, turn on the Slack column to get your notifications as Slack messages.

